# LF everywhere, checked out as LF on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. The shell scripts here run in MSYS2 and in
# Linux (through WSL, which is what judges every pull test), and bash fails on
# a script with CRLF line endings in ways that read as a syntax error in the
# script rather than a line-ending problem. Every script this repository sends
# into WSL had to be filtered through `tr -d '\r'` first; pinning LF is the
# fix for the cause.
#
# It also keeps diffs reviewable: a Windows editor that rewrites endings would
# otherwise show every line of a file as changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never touches these.
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.sys   binary
*.msi   binary
*.img   binary
*.vhdx  binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.pyc   binary
